%description:

Tcp.tcpEcnMode:changed -- a new value acts at the next open; the open connection keeps AccECN.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "ECN: "off": no ECN; "passive": answer an ECN-setup SYN (RFC 3168), but
request no ECN in an active open ...; "rfc3168": request and answer ECN; "accecn": request
Accurate ECN (RFC 9768), and answer it and ECN; "accecn-passive": answer Accurate ECN and ECN,
but request nothing. Each connection reads it at its open".

The classes: off (the value of LegacyTcp), passive (the default), rfc3168, accecn,
accecn-passive, and changed (the value changes during the run; the parameter is @mutable).
The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() reads the mode at the open; the SYN of an
active open requests ECN (ECE, CWR) with "rfc3168" and AccECN (AE, CWR, ECE) with "accecn";
a passive connection answers an AccECN SYN with AccECN ("accecn", "accecn-passive"), with
ECN (ECE; "passive", "rfc3168"), or not at all ("off"). This test separates "changed" from the values other than "accecn".

Host under test: host1, which opens a connection to host2 at 0.1 s with "accecn" and sends its
data at 0.6 s; host2 answers AccECN (tcpEcnMode "accecn-passive", a precondition). At 0.5 s,
the test sets tcpEcnMode of host1 to "off", and host1 opens a second connection at 1 s.
Observation: level 1, the first SYN has AE, CWR and ECE; the data of the first connection
reach host2 with ECT(0); the second SYN has no ECN bits.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpEcnMode
%# class: changed
%# value: "accecn"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpTcpEcnModeChanged")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == true && tcp.cwrBit == true && tcp.eceBit == true")
             .describe("the SYN of the first connection")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).setParameter("host1.tcp", "tcpEcnMode", "\"off\"")
                 .describe("tcpEcnMode of host1 becomes \"off\""))
        .once(on("host2.eth[0].mac").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.ecn == 2")
                  .describe("the data of the first connection at host2, with ECT(0)")
                  .within(0.3))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == false && tcp.cwrBit == false && tcp.eceBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN of the second connection")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpTcpEcnModeChanged compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn-passive"
*.host1.app[0].tSend = 0.6s
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[1].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host1.app[1].connectAddress = "host2"
*.host1.app[1].connectPort = 1000
*.host1.app[1].tOpen = 1.0s
*.host1.app[1].tSend = 1.1s
*.host1.app[1].sendBytes = 1000B
*.host1.app[1].tClose = 1000s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpTcpEcnModeChanged: PASS
